{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And into the Ark you shall put the testimony</b>. I do not know why it is repeated, since it has already been stated (Exodus 25:16), \"And you shall put into the Ark the testimony.\" And one may answer that it comes to teach that while the Ark is still without the cover, he shall first put the testimony inside it and afterward put the cover upon it. And so we find that when he erected the Tabernacle, it is stated, \"And he put the testimony into the Ark\" (Exodus 40:20), and afterward, \"And he put the cover upon the Ark above.\" This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 25:21). But if this were a command, it would more naturally imply that after he puts the cover upon the Ark, as he has said, he shall put the testimony into the Ark, for the Ark is called Ark even when the cover is upon it. And furthermore one may also ask: why did he repeat (Exodus 25:22), \"which is upon the Ark of the testimony,\" for it is well known that the cherubim are upon the Ark of the testimony, and what need is there to explain further, given that he has already said, \"from above the cover from between the two cherubim\"?\n\nBut the explanation is that because he commands concerning the cherubim that they shall spread their wings upward (Exodus 25:20), yet he did not state why they should be made at all, nor what function they serve in the Tabernacle, nor why they should be fashioned in this manner, therefore he now says: you shall place the cover with its cherubim — all as one matter upon the Ark from above — for <b>into the Ark you shall put the testimony which I will give you</b>, in order that it may be for Me a throne of glory, for I will meet with you there and cause My Shekhinah to dwell upon them, <b>and I will speak with you from above the cover from between the two cherubim</b>, because it is upon the Ark of the testimony. Now this is like the chariot that Ezekiel saw, for he said, \"This is the living creature that I saw under the Elohim of Israel by the river Chebar, and I knew that they were cherubim\" (Ezekiel 10:20). And therefore He is called \"He who sits upon the cherubim\" (I Samuel 4:4), for they spread their wings to indicate that they are the chariot, the bearers of the Glory, as it is stated (I Chronicles 28:18), \"and the pattern of the chariot, the cherubim of gold spreading out and covering over the Ark of the covenant of YHWH,\" as I have mentioned (in the introduction to Parashat Terumah).\n\nAnd according to the opinion of our Sages (Ḥagigah 13b), they are human forms, from the Aramaic language in which a youth is called \"ravya,\" and with this root he restored the letter kaf, for thus is the name, like כנערים (like youths), to indicate their nature. And if you consider further why their faces were turned one toward another (Exodus 25:20), and why they were hammered out from the same piece of gold as the cover (Exodus 25:18), you will be able to understand that it is fitting for them to spread their wings upward, for they are a supernal throne, covering over the testimony, which is the writing of Elohim (Exodus 32:16). And this is the meaning of \"the pattern of the chariot,\" for the cherubim that Ezekiel saw bearing the Glory are a pattern for the cherubim that are themselves Glory and Splendor, while the cherubim that are in the Tabernacle and in the Temple are a pattern of them, for \"high above the high one watches, and there are yet higher ones above them\" (Ecclesiastes 5:7). And this is the meaning of \"and I knew\" (Ezekiel 10:20) — that he saw in one and knew in the other, and therefore he said, \"they are\" (ibid.). And the enlightened will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "In the phrase מקשה (Exodus 25:18), Ramban refers to the cherubim being hammered from the same block of gold as the cover; the term is rendered literally as 'hammered out from the same piece of gold as the cover.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:17:08.621745150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}